You are given:
- the candidate the Main Agent selected;
- per-class box counts;
- imbalance ratio;
- empty images;
- malformed annotation lines;
- class-name tokens that match no known class.
Your task is to decide whether the data is clean enough
for the results to be trustworthy, and what concrete
preprocessing, sampling or augmentation action this
candidate requires.
Treat the statistics as ground truth.

